title: Typing a note into the folder
pid: 2962c1d2-5168-4cd8-b4d9-83a26ae752ce
body: |2-
  Only what the view drew under a member can be cut from it. A note you
  type into the forks folder in a save (or move there from elsewhere)
  was not drawn there, so nothing was drawn under it: the save hides
  none of its content, whatever you type under it or leave out. Which
  members were drawn the save reads from the graph before the save, with
  your note's forks as they were. Typed claiming, it is forked by your
  note, as any claiming member is; typed claiming nothing, it is not,
  and a note that is no mirror of yours then stands in the folder
  unwarranted. Either way a child you type under it that its list does
  not name joins its content where you own it (see "Adding a child
  under a member as such"), and a child of it your note hides, typed
  under it, is unhidden. The redrawn view shows it as any member: what
  it shows of its content stands under it, and you may cut from it in
  the next save ('tests/members_typed_into_a_forks_folder.rs').
